A||||13||swoods||GT FACIAS Questions||||1||
Z||000000||swoods||08-06-2001||06:27 PM|||| I have a 1984 2m4 and I found a 85 gt and I wanted to take the front and rear facias and the Notchback decklid and install them on the 84 2m4 is this possible and is there anything I should be aware of before I begin?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-06-2001||06:36 PM||||You'll want to get the 85 engine panels as well, otherwise your engine compartment won't be able to vent. If the 85 decklid is different from your 84 as far as spoiler/luggage rack goes, you'll also need to get the decklid springs from the 85.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-06-2001||08:44 PM||||You'll also want the inner fender wells since the ones on a coupe are different than on a GT.<P>Might as well grab the aero parts from each side and each door too while you are at it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||sprnt96||08-06-2001||09:15 PM||||That is the exact same thing I did to my 84SE. there are a ton of little things that need to be done if you really want to do it right...alot more than i expected when i got started!||||reg||1
Z||000004||swoods||08-07-2001||12:18 AM||||Well I hope I do this right and I hope it matches up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||08-07-2001||01:53 AM||||It will match up. You also need the impact absorber things behind the fascias to really do it right.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||sloth85GT||08-07-2001||02:53 AM||||one question though........why would you do such a thing? Please tell me that the GT is toast with no hope so you're just taking the fascias.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif"> <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||swoods||08-07-2001||03:31 AM||||Yes the gt is in the j/y.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sloth85GT||08-07-2001||01:06 PM||||whew okay, you scared me for a second  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif"> <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||7
Z||000009||MD_Fiero||08-07-2001||10:41 PM||||Same question sorta....but as for me...what all do i need in order to just use the GT front bumper on. thanks<P>------------------<BR>-Tyler<BR>   86' Fiero 2m4||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||08-08-2001||12:59 AM||||Front cover, parking lights, inner fender wells, and impact absorber... that should do it I think...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||MD_Fiero||08-08-2001||12:18 PM||||Ok, Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000012||swoods||08-08-2001||04:58 PM||||Well I think I got Everything I need to do the swap I will start doing the swap tommorow hope everthing goes okay I already spend 4 hour at the J/Y today just pulling everything off but I got A really good deal I paid $80 for everything plus some hood vents the only thing i didnt find was a wing.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||08-08-2001||05:10 PM||||swoods,<BR>If you're installing the ground F/X under the doors, there are metal brackets riveted (screwed?) to the sides of the frame under the door. Kind of in the door sills. You'll need those, too. Your coupe doesn't have 'em. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
